From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wireguard: let the DPAA fast path reuse the receive
 bookkeeping (P6, P7)

The DPAA fast path (drivers/net/wireguard/fastpath.c) decrypts data
packets of a peer's current keypair in place in the receive buffer.
Give it the replay check and the receive timers and keep_key_fresh()
of this file through two thin wrappers, so the
packets it decrypts and the packets that take the normal receive path
share one replay window and one set of timers instead of a copy.

Also offer each decrypted, AllowedIPs-checked packet to
wg_fastpath_rx_tail() before napi_gro_receive(): the fast path may send
a flow the stack has already forwarded straight to its egress port (P7,
module parameter wgfp_rx_tail, off by default). Receive statistics are
unchanged.

Both callers of counter_validate() run with bottom halves already off
(wg_packet_rx_poll() and the fast path are NAPI polls), so it takes
the replay-window lock with spin_lock() instead of spin_lock_bh().

Signed-off-by: VyOS LS1046A maintainers <ask20@vyos-ls1046a-build>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireguard/receive.c b/drivers/net/wireguard/receive.c
index eb8851113..c5cc20aa3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireguard/receive.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireguard/receive.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include "messages.h"
 #include "cookie.h"
 #include "socket.h"
+#include "fastpath.h"
 
 #include <linux/ip.h>
 #include <linux/ipv6.h>
@@ -297,7 +298,11 @@ static bool counter_validate(struct noise_replay_counter *counter, u64 their_cou
 	unsigned long index, index_current, top, i;
 	bool ret = false;
 
-	spin_lock_bh(&counter->lock);
+	/* Bottom halves are already off: both callers, wg_packet_rx_poll() and
+	 * the DPAA fast path's wg_fastpath_rx_validate(), run in NAPI poll
+	 * (threaded NAPI polls under local_bh_disable() too).  The _bh pair
+	 * was 1.2% of the fast path's download profile. */
+	spin_lock(&counter->lock);
 
 	if (unlikely(counter->counter >= REJECT_AFTER_MESSAGES + 1 ||
 		     their_counter >= REJECT_AFTER_MESSAGES))
@@ -326,12 +331,28 @@ static bool counter_validate(struct noise_replay_counter *counter, u64 their_cou
 				&counter->backtrack[index]);
 
 out:
-	spin_unlock_bh(&counter->lock);
+	spin_unlock(&counter->lock);
 	return ret;
 }
 
 #include "selftest/counter.c"
 
+/* The DPAA fast path (fastpath.c, P6) decrypts some data packets of the
+ * current keypair itself.  It keeps their replay window and timers on the
+ * same state and code as the packets that come through this file. */
+bool wg_fastpath_rx_validate(struct noise_keypair *keypair, u64 nonce)
+{
+	return counter_validate(&keypair->receiving_counter, nonce);
+}
+
+void wg_fastpath_rx_timers(struct wg_peer *peer)
+{
+	keep_key_fresh(peer);
+	wg_timers_any_authenticated_packet_received(peer);
+	wg_timers_any_authenticated_packet_traversal(peer);
+	wg_timers_data_received(peer);
+}
+
 static void wg_packet_consume_data_done(struct wg_peer *peer,
 					struct sk_buff *skb,
 					struct endpoint *endpoint)
@@ -408,7 +429,9 @@ static void wg_packet_consume_data_done(struct wg_peer *peer,
 	if (unlikely(routed_peer != peer))
 		goto dishonest_packet_peer;
 
-	napi_gro_receive(&peer->napi, skb);
+	/* the DPAA fast path may forward a learned flow directly (P7) */
+	if (!wg_fastpath_rx_tail(peer, skb))
+		napi_gro_receive(&peer->napi, skb);
 	update_rx_stats(peer, message_data_len(len_before_trim));
 	return;
 
-- 
